final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_sj1xv")
province = 43
blurb = "This print depicts the famous funabashi (floating bridge) of Toyama in Etchū Province (modern-day Toyama prefecture), which was constructed using boats to cross the Jinzu River.

The bridge was set up by the ruling Maeda clan around 1639 by chaining 64 riverboats together and laying wooden planks over them to form a roadway.

The bridge was highly dynamic. During heavy rains or spring snowmelt from the Japanese Alps, the river's current would become too strong. To prevent the bridge from being destroyed, officials would temporarily dismantle it, unchaining the boats and securing them to the banks until the waters receded."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
